      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed study spans 25–80 °C, 0.1–3 wt.% NaCl, and pH 2–7.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The governing structural mediator is the formation and subsequent breakdown of a partial oxide or passivation layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6427115::web::016::4_2_corrosion_resistance"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interfacial pH changes govern the stability of the surface film.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chloride drives pitting and breakdown of the surface film.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
